WEBVTT

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.160
Hey, Umaru.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.870
What kind of cake should we have for Christmas?

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.410
I'm hanging out with friends this year,

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.410
so don't worry about it. 

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.200
O-oh... 

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:23.500
Big Brother! If you're gonna make a cake again next year,

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:23.500
you should make a Santa doll too!

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.040
SADNESS

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:27.910
LONELINESS

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:27.910
SADNESS

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:30.120
LONELINESS

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:30.120
SADNESS

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:30.120
DESPAIR

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:33.120
On second thought, I WILL have cake

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:33.120
on the 25th so go on, make one!

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.330
R-really?

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.750
December 24th

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:13.870
Episode 4: A Party with the Gang

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.160
Dude, you're making a cake from scratch?

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.870
You're better than most DADS. 

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.290
Well, I enjoy it...

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:20.950
Taihei, if little Tanukichi wasn't around,

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:20.950
you'd have nothing to do and just shrivel up, huh?

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.250
Anyway, it looks like we won't have to work

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.250
overtime today, so how about we go somewhere?

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.750
And you're overdue to join us, Alex.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.080
I'm going to a Christmas concert of anime songs.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.080
Would you like to come with me?

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.370
Tanoshiku nareba ii desu wa

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.370
If you can enjoy yourself, that will be good indeed!

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:39.910
Woo-hoo!

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.120
Sore nara kitto kachi desu wa

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.120
Do that, and you're sure to win indeed!

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:42.910
Woo-hoo!

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:45.120
Just us three?

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:51.290
Christmas will be kinda boring without Tanukichi around.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.450
No, we SHOULD go to that concert. 

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.450
Huh? For real?

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.450
Yes, please!

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.370
O-okay...

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:13.830
It's Christmas indeed!

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.330
Where should we go?

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.540
I-I'm fine with wherever!

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:21.750
Hey, Ebina, you're okay with not

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:21.750
going back to Akita this year?

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:23.370
Yes, it's fine.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:27.620
I've gone back because

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:27.620
I felt sad ringing in the new year alone...

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:31.580
But with all the fun we've been having together,

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:31.580
I haven't felt lonely at all. 

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:33.370
And we shall have fun indeed!

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.040
The reason being... it is indeed Christmas!

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:39.830
Sylphin is pretty excited, huh?

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:39.830
It's Christmas! Christmas! Indeed!

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.200
What a child...

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.200
It's Christmas! Christmas! Indeed!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.250
Don't you celebrate Christmas at home?

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.250
Now you, Ebina!

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:45.830
Um, correct! We do not!

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:45.830
"It's Christmas"!

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.080
Oh, really?

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.160
It's Christmas day...

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:53.160
I'm spending Christmas with Umaru!

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.620
WOO-HOO!

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.330
Hey, do you want to go see the lights?

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:02.700
Wow...!

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:04.750
These are pretty indeed!

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:06.660
Still...

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.080
It's nothing but couples here. 

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:10.200
Yeah...

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:17.540
Ah! They're dressed like Santa!

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:18.370
You're right!

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.410
They're selling cakes. And...

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:22.950
This tight miniskirt will make you

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:22.950
one cute Santa Claus

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:23.620
they're even selling costumes. 

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.450
LONELINESS

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.450
SADNESS

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.450
DESPAIR

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.410
Big Brother sure looked pretty sad...

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:40.660
Kyou kara holiday! Mankitsu shichae!

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:40.660
Our holiday starts today! Enjoy it to the fullest!

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:43.450
This is way more fun than I thought it would be, Alex!

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:45.120
I know, right?!

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.120
Three-day weekend!

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.830
I-I don't really follow...

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.120
Wherever you go, there are so many people... 

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.870
Everyone wants to do something on Christmas, right?

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:59.790
So, do none of you have a special someone

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:59.790
with whom to spend this time?

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.160
Ebina, do you have someone?

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:06.040
Huh?! N-no, I don't! 

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:08.080
What about you, Kirie?

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.200
O-o-of course I don't!

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:14.410
In that case, why don't we all go back to my house?

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:17.000
We'll have a Christmas party!

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:21.000
I thought we were going to talk about relationships,

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:21.000
but she was just inviting us over...

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:30.910
Here we are indeed!

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.450
Someone spent a LOT of time decorating...

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:37.250
The type that gets VERY nervous

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:37.250
when entering a new home

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.500
Kirie, are you all right?

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.330
I-I-I... I think so!

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.160
You can sit where you like, indeed!

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:46.370
Huh? There's an extra cushion. 

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.870
Ah! Actually, one more person will be joining us!

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:51.200
Could she mean... Alex?

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:55.580
I've invited my good friend UMR!

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:56.790
What?!

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:58.870
Oh, really?

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.750
Wh-who is that?

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.040
UMR?

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:08.910
The champion of the gaming world!

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:08.910
And the person who gave me this badge!

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:12.870
WINNER

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:12.790
Oh, that badge is from a game?

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.200
UMR is SO cool!

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:16.830
Is it a guy?

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:21.120
What should I do? Did I promise to meet her today?

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:26.620
And it's thanks to UMR that we were able

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:26.620
to get together like this today!

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:32.330
I haven't had many friends since coming to Japan. 

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:38.450
Even after enrolling in school,

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:38.450
I had little idea indeed as to how to make friends. 

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:45.660
But then, I learned the Japanese custom of

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:45.660
making friends by challenging others and beating them!

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:49.580
WORLD

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:49.580
CHAMPIONSHIPS

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.500
Something's not right here!

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:54.950
I wanted to make friends with Umaru,

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:54.950
which is why I challenged her at school.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:07:05.660
But it was UMR who taught me... you don't make friends

00:06:56.540 --> 00:07:05.660
by beating them, you do it by having FUN with them.

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:10.200
And the strength of that becomes a dream

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:10.200
that will lead to the future!

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:12.290
Did I ever say that?!

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:17.500
It was UMR's advice that let me

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:17.500
become friends with you all!

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:29.580
It was a lesson well learned:

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:29.580
If something is bothering you, just ask for advice.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.120
Otherwise, you will regret it!

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:38.830
There are indeed many, many things

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:38.830
for UMR and I to discuss!

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:51.620
AAAAA

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:51.620
SHPAAAAAA

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.540
S

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.540
H

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.540
P

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.540
A                                                      AAAAAAAA

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:13.700
I'm sure she's worn out.

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:15.790
And I bet...

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.950
she decorated this room all by herself. 

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:22.870
Let's make sure not to wake her as we leave. 

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:23.790
Okay.

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:26.950
Hold on a second. 

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:31.700
Oh! Me too!

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.660
And YOU, Kirie. 

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.950
O-oh... O-o-o-okay!

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:41.620
Well, till next time.  

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.370
Ah! I had a lot of fun today!

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:57.200
Text

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:57.200
Text Received

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.830
From Sylphin...? She woke up?

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.500
U.M.R!

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.500
I'm about to have a party at my house.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.500
Why not stop by, if you'd like?

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:01.660
This was sent two hours ago...

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:05.750
Oh! All these texts being sent

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:05.750
on Christmas must be causing delays. 

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:08.370
Is something wrong, Umaru?

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:11.040
No, not at all. 

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:15.500
UMR is SO cool! SO cool! SO COOL!

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:22.790
Sorry, Ebina. I left something at Sylphin's house.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:22.790
Are you okay going home alone?

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:24.410
S-sure!

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.540
Sorry!

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:37.250
Huh? Ebina?

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:41.080
T-Taihei!

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:44.290
Weren't you supposed to hang out with Umaru today?

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:50.370
Oh! I was, up until a little while ago.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:50.370
But she said she forgot something, so...

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:54.160
I can't believe she just left you on your own.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.620
No, I'm perfectly fine!

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:58.450
How about we go back together?

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.290
O-okay!

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:14.250
Mom! Look, a couple!

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:16.540
Stop that! 

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:26.830
U-um...

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:31.790
It's just, I... I... I...

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:34.910
I'm sorry for putting you out like this. 

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.290
No, don't worry about it.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:39.870
It's dangerous to be out alone at night, right?

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:46.410
If something is bothering you, just ask for advice.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:48.160
Otherwise, you will regret it!

00:10:55.700 --> 00:11:00.000
Um, there's something I'd like to talk to you about.

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:06.500
It's...

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.700
It's Santa!

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:15.330
Well hello there, Sylphin! Merry Christmas!

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:15.330
Now then, tell me what you'd like for a present. Anything!

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:17.330
Ho-ho-ho!

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:18.500
Really?!

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:22.870
In that case, I... I would like some Japanese friends!

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:26.450
Huh...?

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:30.160
Oh? So, that's what you wished for?

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:30.250
On House Patrol

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.750
Santa seemed most disturbed!

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.910
The old man... I mean, even Santa

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.910
couldn't make FRIENDS happen, huh?

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:42.620
But, I want some friends

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:42.620
I can talk to about Japan, indeed!

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:47.080
Just ask for a computer once you're in middle school. 

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:51.370
You can talk to people from Japan

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:51.370
just by using the internet. 

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:52.620
Is this true?!

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:59.620
Shinra Rasenken Sirius

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:59.620
Real men stain themselves with darkness...

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:54.790
Look.

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:59.580
This is my Japanese friend, Shinra Rasenken Sirius. 

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:01.750
That's an impressive name indeed!

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:06.750
On House Patrol

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:03.500
And I'll be able to meet him soon. 

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:06.750
Huh? Brother, you're going to Japan?

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:10.410
Yup. I'll be going to high school there. 

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.910
School... in Japan?

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:27.870
I'm sure you'll be a little sad when Alex leaves. 

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:30.450
You two have always been close...

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:33.000
Big Brother!

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.790
Yo, Alex!

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.790
This vid is awesome,

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.790
so check it out!

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:42.750
Brother's friend...?

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:49.500
UMH is unstoppable!

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:51.660
That is one fearsome Japanese fighter!

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:56.830
WORLD

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:56.830
CHAMPIONSHIPS

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.080
This hard-fought battle has forged mutual respect! 

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.540
By challenging others, one can make friends...

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.580
such admirable fighting spirit!

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:07.700
Merry Christmas, Sylphin!

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:07.700
Here, it's a fighting game controller!

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:10.040
Indeed, made by HORU!

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:15.700
She sure has started to want some strange things...

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:18.870
Thank you so much, Santa!

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.750
Huh? Santa?

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.370
Oh, no. I fell asleep. 

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:29.620
What...?

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:33.330
Today was

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:33.330
so much fun,

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:33.330
Sylphin!

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:33.120
Today was so much fun, Sylphin!

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:36.450
I was very happy

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:36.450
that you invited me.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:35.620
I was very happy that you invited me.

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:38.160
M-m-merry Christmash!

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:38.750
Merry Christmas

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:43.620
I guess they've all gone home. 

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:45.250
Sylphin!

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:56.750
Merry Christmas, TSF.

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:01.120
Santa...? UMR, why are you dressed like that?

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:06.700
Well, I saw them selling these,

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:06.700
so... d-does it look okay on me? 

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:13.540
I'm sorry I'm late. Um, do you mind if I come in?

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:18.000
I want a Japanese friend indeed!

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:19.660
Yes!

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.330
Happy New Year...

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.200
Happy...

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:40.290
January 1st

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:43.830
New Year's

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:43.830
Allowance

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.330
Here. For you. 

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.410
WOO-HOO!

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:56.870
Thanks, Big Brother! It's not like you

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:56.870
to hand this out first thing in the morning!

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.370
Uh... sure.  

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:04.200
Huh? Is he still half-asleep?

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:06.450
Well, let's eat!

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:07.620
Let's eat. 

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:12.000
Oh, yeah... 

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.160
Here, Umaru. It's your New Year's allowance. 

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.250
New Year's

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.250
Allowance

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:19.290
Wh-what sorcery is this?!

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:23.000
New Year's

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:23.000
Allowance

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:22.870
Am I being tested?

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.700
What's wrong? You don't seem happy at all. 

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:27.580
Ah!

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:30.120
Thank you, Big Brother!

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:33.120
RRRRRRRUMBLE

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:33.120
New Year's

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:33.120
Allowance

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:33.120
New Year's

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:33.120
Allowance

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:33.040
I got TWO of them...

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:36.580
and I sure am grateful!

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:41.370
It's like when a vending machine messes up

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:41.370
and gives you two drinks instead of one. 

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:46.250
Would you, dear Consumer, pay for both?

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:48.160
No, you wouldn't!

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:51.160
This mistake is all on my brother!

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:52.120
The thing is...

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:54.160
Take yer average ramen shop.

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:58.120
What if you order one bowl but you friggin' get TWO?

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.540
I sure feel lucky to have gotten two!

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:04.700
Thanks, that was great!

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.120
But you gotta pay for that other one, right?

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:10.620
Otherwise, the fault now lies with YOU!

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:12.160
Hold it right there!

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.910
Think about game arcades! 

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:20.120
If I put in one coin but end up getting two prizes,

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:20.120
they're both still mine!  

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:22.160
That's just the nature of the game, right?

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:24.870
And life is like a game, right?!

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:27.290
"Life" is about goals and aimin' for the top!

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:28.870
Life is Cannalad!

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:33.950
More to the point, why would Big Brother

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:33.950
have prepared TWO envelopes?

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:38.160
Yeah, he should only need one, right? 

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:39.450
That's true...

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:45.950
Ah-ha! This whole time, something has felt off.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:45.950
Two envelopes... Big Brother spacing out... 

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:48.080
It can only mean...!

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:49.410
"Can only mean"?!

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:55.870
That he'd planned on giving two

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:55.870
New Year's allowances all along!

00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:58.750
Guess I'll give her two this year. 

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:00.700
Wh-what was that?!

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:06.160
Big Brother...?

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:13.120
Oh, Ebina. 

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:16.540
Um, Happy New Year. 

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:18.500
Happy New Year. 

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:23.830
U-um, I hope I can be of help to you this year as well.

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:26.160
Yeah, same here. 

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:27.660
Um-!

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:35.410
U-um... i-is Umaru here?

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:38.410
Yes, but... she's still asleep. 

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:42.910
Hey, I'm awake! These two are acting WEIRD! 

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:45.750
Oh! I have a New Year's gift for you.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:49.000
Huh?! N-no, I couldn't!

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.410
It's no trouble. Hold on a second. 

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:57.200
Let's see...

00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:03.370
Huh? That's strange. I put it right here, next to Umaru's.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:09.120
La-la-laaa...

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:15.290
Sorry it's not in an envelope.

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:19.790
Ebina said she's going to check out the New Year's sales.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:21.910
O-oh.

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:27.660
Um, Big Brother? Let's talk about vending machines...

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.450
She

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.450
gave

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.450
it

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.450
back

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:32.450
INNOCENT

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:41.450
Huh? Where did Taihei go?

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:43.830
He got called to the meeting room a little while ago. 

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:46.870
The meeting room? That's unusual. 

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:48.870
He seemed quite happy, though. 

00:18:54.790 --> 00:18:56.870
Huh? Your brother said that?

00:18:57.080 --> 00:19:01.540
Yeah. He gets all mad if I leave even a small mess.   

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:05.620
By a "small mess," does she mean...?

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.410
Come on, Umaru, you need to put this away. 

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:10.540
It really was small. 

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:13.870
Umaru! I told you to clean up after yourself!

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:16.000
He really is too strict. 

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:17.290
Still...

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:23.040
he's a good listener, and he's really kind.  

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:25.040
Huh? A "listener"?

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:27.370
Ah! N-no, never mind. 

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:30.160
Ebina sure is nice...

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:33.000
All Big Brother ever does is get mad! 

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:39.870
Still, that's not to say I'm entirely without fault...

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:51.830
Huh? It turns out Big Brother is SUPER nice!

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.660
On the other hand, I'm just...

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:59.450
Get me some cola and potato chips.

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:59.450
Oh, and more manga, okay?

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:01.750
Yup, I ate yours too!

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:04.540
Come on! Just one more billing charge!

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:07.160
I might... actually be selfish!

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:13.540
From the outside looking in,

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:13.540
all I do is push Big Brother around!

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:16.910
This is bad... I have to do something!

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:21.450
I'm home.

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:24.370
Welcome back, Big Brother!

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:26.870
I'm sure you've had a long day at work!

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:28.540
Wait, what's going on? 

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:30.830
Come on, just have a seat...

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:31.870
Umaruuuuun!

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:35.410
and welcome to the Umaru-style Space of Happiness!

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:37.620
Hurry up and step right in, Big Brother!

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:41.450
Umaru, I need to talk to you. 

00:20:41.870 --> 00:20:42.620
Huh?

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:45.080
I have to go on a business trip.

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:49.500
Huh...?

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:53.500
So you... you won't be coming back? 

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:58.620
Yeah. I got chosen as a member of the project team,

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:58.620
and I'll have to go out of town.  

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:00.330
I won't be able to come back here for a while. 

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:10.620
No! You can't leave me, Big Brother!

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:11.910
I'm sorry.

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:16.500
No! You can't just leave and not come back!

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:21.160
I'm sorry, Umaru. I'm worried about this too,

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:21.160
but the decision has been made. 

00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:27.500
How long will you be gone? A month? Wait, a year?!

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:28.410
Two...

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:29.700
Two weeks. 

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:35.250
Two weeks...?

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:39.750
Yeah. If I'm gone for two weeks,

00:21:35.410 --> 00:21:39.750
you'll make a real mess around here, right?

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:44.000
THAT'S WHAT YOU'RE WORRIED ABOUT?! 

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:47.160
And, wait! What makes you think I'll make a mess?!

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:48.790
You always do, right?

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:55.410
Yeah, but... look, just get out and stay gone,

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:55.410
for at least two weeks!

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:27.330
Next Episode

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:27.330
Preview

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:29.830
Tanukichi! It sure is fun to enjoy Christmas

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:29.830
with some anime songs, right?!

00:23:27.330 --> 00:23:41.000
Next Episode

00:23:27.330 --> 00:23:41.000
Preview

00:23:27.330 --> 00:23:41.000
Episode 5: Big Brother Departs

00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:31.790
Bomba, you finally get it, huh?

00:23:31.790 --> 00:23:35.330
I GET TO ENJOY THE SEASON EVEN THOUGH

00:23:31.790 --> 00:23:35.330
I DON'T HAVE A GIRLFRIEND!

00:23:35.330 --> 00:23:36.620
IS ANYONE OUT THERE LISTENING?! 

00:23:36.620 --> 00:23:40.330
Stop that! There are people crying

00:23:36.620 --> 00:23:40.330
in front of their TVs right now! 
